# What `docker build` must NEVER copy into an image layer.
#
# Same reasoning as backend/.dockerignore: the Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, and
# `.env.local` is where RAG_API_KEY lives locally. An image layer is a
# distributable artifact — a key baked into one is readable with `docker history`,
# and no amount of runtime env-passing takes it back out.
#
# The UI's whole security property is that the browser never sees a key. That
# property is worth exactly nothing if the key ships in the image instead.

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- Rebuilt inside the image; copying them in wastes layers and can poison the
# --- build with a host-built cache (wrong platform, stale routes).
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/

# --- Build/dev cruft ---------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.DS_Store
*.log
npm-debug.log*
coverage/
